 "description": "Deterministic matching cases. Each one states, per requirement, the verdict a careful person would reach from the profile alone — not the verdict the current rules happen to produce. Where those differ, the rules are what should change. Coverage here is of SHAPES of judgment (alias, near-miss, duration, field-of-study, credential level, sparsity), not of volume: a hundred perfect matches would score well and teach nothing.\n\nForked from matching_v1 when the rules gained graded evidence. Exactly one expectation changed: a technology demonstrated in a paid role's description now MATCHES a requirement that does not demand production use, where matching_v1 called it UNCERTAIN because the skills list did not repeat it. That change came from the real-data benchmark, where it was the single largest class of disagreement with human judgment. matching_v1/cases.json is kept beside this file so the older rules stay interpretable.",
